    39	## 2. From JAC-FIBRE to the exact local identity
    40	
    41	### 2.1 What JAC-FIBRE really gives
    42	
    43	Let `g(x,tau_i(x)) = c_2` on a simple branch of a generic fibre. Then
    44	
    45	```text
    46	g_x + g_y tau_i' = 0,
    47	d/dx f(x,tau_i) = f_x + f_y tau_i' = (f_x g_y - f_y g_x)/g_y = c/g_y.
    48	```
    49	
    50	Thus, for a pre-existing Keller pair,
    51	
    52	```text
    53	f(x,tau_i(x)) = c integral dx/g_y(x,tau_i(x)) + a_i.
    54	```
    55	
    56	This is the exact series identity behind the promoted valuation statement
    57	`I17:14-17` and `D1:203-214`. Since `g-c_2` is monic with `n` distinct generic
    58	roots and `deg_y f=m<n`, `f` is indeed the unique degree-`<n` Lagrange
    59	interpolant through these `n` values. That global programme is stated at
    60	`I17:94-100`.
    61	
    62	Now put
    63	
    64	```text
    65	x=t^(-1),                 y=w(t)+pi t^delta,
    66	F(t,pi)=f(x,y),           G(t,pi)=g(x,y).
    67	```
    68	
    69	The change-of-variables determinant is
    70	
   230	`c(d+e)/(d(1-delta_1)) = c e/q`.
   231	
