   236	### 4.3 The sum identities
   237	
   238	Because `deg p_f<deg p_g` and `p_g` is squarefree, partial fractions and (4.1)
   239	give
   240	
   241	```text
   242	p_f(pi)/p_g(pi)
   243	 = sum_i [p_f(c_i)/p_g'(c_i)]/(pi-c_i)
   244	 = (kappa/d) sum_{k>=0} pi^(-k-1)
   245	       sum_i c_i^k/p_g'(c_i)^2.                              (4.2)
   246	```
   247	
   248	The left side first appears at power `pi^[-(a_1-b_1)]`. Hence
   249	
   250	```text
   251	sum_i c_i^k/p_g'(c_i)^2 = 0,
   252	      0 <= k <= a_1-b_1-2=(e-d)V_2-2,
   253	
   254	sum_i c_i^(a_1-b_1-1)/p_g'(c_i)^2
   255	      = (d/kappa)(lc p_f/lc p_g) != 0.                       (4.3)
   256	```
   257	
   258	The first range is empty when its upper endpoint is negative. This exactly
   259	confirms `TF:394-410` and the user's stated range.
   260	
   261	Verdict STAR-SUM: **CONFIRMED — CAN promote.**
