    15	- **Grok §4 (the "Wronskian dictionary")** and **Sol §2 (the "D₁
    16	  self-different")**: along a root τ_i of g − c₂, implicit
    17	  differentiation with [f,g] = ±1 gives d/dx f(x,τ_i) = ±1/g_y(x,τ_i),
    18	  and g monic gives g_y(τ_i) = ∏_{j≠i}(τ_i − τ_j). Hence the pole of f
    19	  along τ_i is EXACTLY 1 + Σ_{j≠i} ord_t(τ_i − τ_j) = 1 − δ⁰_i, and
    20	     N = Σ_i (1 − δ⁰_i)⁺     over the roots of g − c₂        (DICT-N)
    21	  is a function of the g-tree ALONE; the f-tree is slaved, not free.
    22	- **Sol §2 (SD3–SD6)** and **the coordinator (EXACT-N, launched as a
    23	  hostile flagship before Sol was opened)**: the frontier bound gives
    24	  pole_i ≥ 1 − δ₁ + λ_g(δ₁) = d(1−δ₁)/(d+e) (RADIUS-ORDER at r = 1),
    25	  while FRONTIER-N with monotonicity gives pole_i ≤ −λ_f(δ₁) =
    26	  d(1−δ₁)/(d+e). EQUALITY is forced: the sub-tree of every bottom-major
    27	  disc is a STAR, and
    28	     N = Σ_{bottom-major B} eV₂(B) · d(1 − δ₁(B))/(d + e),
    29	     Σ_B eV₂(B) ≤ ue.                                        (EXACT-N)
    30	  Deeper g–g contact RAISES N (the opposite of integration #16 §C).
