+# Blind full-spectrum ideation — 20260903T1015Z — Sol 5.6
+
+## 0. Custody, scope, and direct verdict
+
+I verified the charged packet before reading any banked report:
+
+```text
+99c940d1167acfc7796436457a1d87bdd0a1a1a4c673c7bb2e0d3436e3d086b7  /tmp/jc2-lane.F6oSte/inputs/ideation-20260903T1015Z-packet.md
+```
+
+It matched.  I did not read another `ideation-20260903T1015Z-*`
+submission, any of the three in-progress lane reports named in the packet, or
+`jc2-lean`, and I have not edited a canonical ledger.  I did read the now-present
+primary source
+`refs/moh1983_jram340_configurations_of_roots.pdf`; its SHA-256 is
+`6c8847a8d8374f7d7725c7e2ede2895a2c30034af6a7f28c511a471c41aa6a51`.
+In particular I inspected pp. 148--153, 179--189, 198--202, and Appendices I--II,
+pp. 203--212.  Thus claims below about what Moh prints are primary-source claims;
+claims about what his lost or unpublished program actually did remain
+source-unverified.
+
+**Direct verdict.**  Stop treating the boundary count as the prospective
+all-degree engine.  It has done its job: it computes the fixed Keller degree
+`N` exactly, and that value is `O(1)`.  Worse for a purely numerical programme,
+the printed Moh conditions (1)--(13), together with formal (UNI) pinned
+integrality, admit an explicit unbounded family with **exactly `N=6`**.  The
+all-degree programme must therefore attack *global realisability*: whether the
+local branch data are the restrictions of one polynomial `g` and whether the
+fibrewise primitive of `1/g_y` is one polynomial `f`.  The right object is a
+finite quotient-algebra connection/observability problem, not another cap on
+the number of boundary contacts.
+
+This does not demote the exact boundary theorem.  `D1-PIN` is the indispensable
+bridge that turns a hypothetical counterexample into a sharply typed formal
+packet.  It simply cannot turn bounded `N` into bounded `D`; that is already the
+binding `PIN-NOT-CEILING` conclusion (`AUDIT.md:15270-15284`; `notes.md:20645-20679`).
+The census is likewise a target generator and regression suite, not a proof by
+eventual exhaustion.
+
+## 1. What the all-degree program should be
+
+The programme should be stated without euphemism:
+
+> Given a Moh (1)--(13) skeleton and a formally integral bottom packet with
+> `N >= 6`, prove that no single pair `f,g in C[x,y]` realises its complete
+> branch tower and the identity `f_x g_y-f_y g_x=1`; or construct such a pair.
+
+There are three layers, and every future lane should say which layer it tests.
+
+1. **Numerical admissibility.**  Moh's divisibility chain, radii, Galois choices,
+   bottom packet capacity and exact pinned `N`.  This is fast and useful, but it
+   is only a superset of actual maps.  The rebased census has 14,016 groups
+   through `D=200` and empties no degree above 100
+   (`xmodel/census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md:894-924`).
+2. **Branch-packet realisability.**  Approximate-root/semigroup data must assemble
+   the flags, conjugate factors and bottom dessins into the branch packet of one
+   polynomial `g`.  This is where Moh's unexplained 658-to-6 reduction and the
+   orbit interpretation of (10)/(11) belong.  A root orbit, a geometric disc,
+   and a cover series are three different objects until an injection or quotient
+   map is proved.
+3. **Global Keller mate.**  On a generic fibre `g=c`, the equation is
+   `D_g f := g_y f_x-g_x f_y=1`.  It must have a solution with the prescribed
+   bidegree/total-degree support, simultaneously on all branches and at infinity.
+   Local no-log solutions, a representative bottom star, and vanishing of one
+   residue are necessary, not attainment.
+
+The computational core for layers 2--3 should be exact linear algebra over a
+function field.  Put
+
+```text
+K = Q(x,c),                    h(y) = g(x,y)-c,
+B = K[y]/(h),                  rank_K B = n,
+nabla = partial_x - (g_x/g_y) partial_y,
+W_m = span_K(1,y,...,y^(m-1)), C : B -> B/W_m.
+```
+
+Here `g_y` is inverted only on the squarefree generic fibre; exceptional
+discriminant components must be split off explicitly.  A Keller mate is a vector
+`F in W_m` satisfying `nabla F=1/g_y`, together with the polynomial-in-`x`
+and degree constraints that distinguish `C[x,y]` from `K[y]`.  Differentiate
+`C(F)=0`, substitute the connection equation, and prolong.  This produces an
+inhomogeneous observability/Krylov matrix.  Its left kernel gives compatibility
+functionals on `g`; its rank defect gives the only places where a candidate can
+survive.  For the `D=105` shape `(n,m)=(105,70)`, the first projection already
+has `105-70=35` output coordinates: at each genuine exponent there can be up to
+35 compatibility equations before new coefficients of `g` and gauge freedom
+are counted.
+
+This formulation unifies several banked ideas that had been pursued separately:
+Lagrange interpolation on the 105 roots, Hermite/Bezoutian trace identities,
+the Hamiltonian derivation `D_g`, the Brieskorn/Gauss--Manin viewpoint, and
+linear-systems observability.  It also gives a machine filter with a proof
+certificate: a nonzero exact minor or a left-kernel functional whose numerator
+cannot vanish under the skeleton's leading data.  Numerical rank is only a
+candidate detector; every promoted obstruction must be recovered over `Q` (or
+by enough primes plus rational reconstruction) and checked on the correct ideal
+component.
+
+The resulting campaign is not “search degrees until the list becomes empty.”
+It is: derive a **uniform rank/semigroup obstruction** on a symbolic family, use
+the `D=105` trio as the smallest honest unit tests, and use surviving symbolic
+rays as adversarial inputs.  If the obstruction is uniform, it proves the
+theorem.  If it repeatedly lifts a ray, it is the shortest route toward an
+actual counterexample attempt.
+
+## 2. Answers to Q1–Q4
+
+### 2.1 Q1 — Moh's missing elimination
+
+Moh's p. 201 prints (1)--(13), and p. 202 says that the discussion can be put
+into a computer program and then displays six outputs.  The paper does **not**
+print code or a further scalar predicate explaining the jump from the 658 rows
+reproduced by `box/moh_skeleton_full.py` to those six.  Appendix II starts with
+the six outputs and eliminates them case by case; it does not account for the
+652 earlier eliminations.  The primary text also openly stresses, before the
+search, that the intermediate `M_i` are not known a priori.  Therefore the
+coordinator's phrase “Moh's missing condition” is too confident.  The live
+alternatives are: an omitted program gate, a richer use of Propositions 5.3/5.6
+or approximate roots that was never summarized as a numbered condition, or an
+error/incompleteness in the 1983 computation.  We should try to falsify the
+table, not reverse-engineer it under an assumption of infallibility.
+
+I ran a cheap hypothesis-mining pass over the exact 658-row reproduction.  Two
+natural predicates are unexpectedly sharp:
+
+```text
+predicate                                      rows       (n,m) classes
+M_2 > n-d_2                                      57              16
+choose printed nonzero branch (10) at every j   156              40
+both predicates                                  10               6
+Moh's printed table                               6               6
+```
+
+All six printed rows survive the conjunction.  It removes 648 of 652 excess
+rows and leaves only four extras:
+
+```text
+(n,m)       M-chain       V_2,V_3
+(96,64)     (68,94)       2,3
+(96,64)     (76,94)       3,3
+(96,64)     (72,94)       2,7
+(100,40)    (88,98)       3,3
+```
+
+At `(75,50)` it has exactly the requested discrimination: it removes
+`M_2 in {5,10,40,60}` and retains `M_2=55` with `V_2 in {2,3}`.  This is a
+**measured clue, not a theorem**.  In particular, forcing (10) is not licensed
+merely because Proposition 5.6 says that (11) “cannot always happen,” and the
+inequality `M_2>n-d_2` needs a line-by-line source derivation.  The experiment's
+value is that it reduces source forensics to ten witnesses: reconstruct the
+factor data for these ten from Propositions 5.3 and 5.6 and Appendix II, and ask
+which exact assertion kills the last four.
+
+`OPEN[MOH-PROGRAM]` remains the correct label.  **Bounded quantity:** 652 excess
+rows in 59 excess `(n,m)` classes at `n<=100`; the immediate `P202-10` audit is
+the ten rows above (six positive controls, four negative targets).  The original
+bounded definition and the required `(75,50)` controls are in
+`xmodel/census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md:957-970`.
+
+Decisive outcomes are deliberately symmetric.  If the source proves both
+predicates and a rule killing the four extras, implement that rule independently
+and run it symbolically on the unbounded family below.  If the source proves the
+gate but the family survives, Moh's gate is a sieve, not the all-degree theorem.
+If neither predicate can be sourced, reject the attractive fit and record that
+the p. 202 six-row assertion has not been independently reproduced.  No branch
+choice is to be silently promoted because it matches the table.
+
+### 2.2 Q2 — the `D = 105` trio
+
+All three groups have `(n,m,K,d,e,V_2)=(105,70,35,2,3,1)` and hence the
+same order-zero cubic dessin, after affine/scalar normalization:
+
+```text
+p_g(pi)=pi^3-pi,       p_f(pi)=pi^2-2/3.
+```
+
+Order zero cannot distinguish them and cannot kill them.  The useful arithmetic
+is instead:
+
+| group | `(M_2,V_3)` | `delta_2` | `delta_1` | `q` | formal packets in `6<=N<=16` |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| A | `(28,5)` | `7/18` | `7/12` | `1/2` | `k=12,14,16,18,20,22,24` |
+| B | `(28,6)` | `2/13` | `11/26` | `9/13` | `k=13` |
+| C | `(40,4)` | `4/17` | `19/34` | `9/17` | `k=17` |
+
+Thus there are nine formal (UNI) packet cases, not merely three rows.  “Formal”
+is essential: `k` records a numerical choice within the bottom capacity; it is
+not a count of proved actual exits or an attainment statement.
+
+The cheapest exact global discriminator avoids constructing a 105-term
+Lagrange polynomial.  For monic `h(z)=g(x,z)-c=prod_i(z-tau_i)` and branch
+primitives `I_i`, let `H` be their degree-`<105` interpolant and set
+
+```text
+S_r = sum_i I_i tau_i^r / h'(tau_i).
+```
+
+The partial-fraction identity
+
+```text
+H(z)/h(z) = sum_i I_i/[h'(tau_i)(z-tau_i)]
+          = sum_(r>=0) S_r z^(-r-1)
+```
+
+shows that a **monic degree-70** mate satisfies exactly 34 degree vanishings
+`S_0=...=S_33=0` and one normalization `S_34=1`.  At every positive Puiseux
+order, the corresponding 35 equations are homogeneous.  This is a differential
+generalized Reed--Solomon parity check.  It is equivalent to projecting the
+quotient-algebra solution `F` to its 34 forbidden high-`y` coordinates and its
+one leading coordinate.  The fibre primitive and global interpolation identity
+are exact (`xmodel/time-function-endgame-review-sol56-20260902.md:43-60`), while
+the same review warns that local completed-series membership is not global
+polynomiality (`ibid.:103-130`).
+
+This supplies the requested condition count, but **not** an honest unknown
+count before the full branch packet and exponent support are supplied.  The
+restricted bottom operator has seven coefficient unknowns and five equations:
+generic rank 5, kernel 2, cokernel 0; at `E in {mu,2mu,3mu}` it has rank 4,
+kernel 3, cokernel 1.  That is a local associated-graded calculation, not the
+global count.  Outer roots already enlarge the coefficient spaces and the
+first-exponent semigroup has not been established
+(`xmodel/time-function-endgame-review-sol56-20260902.md:489-520,574-607`).
+Accordingly, a lane that prints “unknowns minus conditions” without those two
+inputs has not answered Q2.
+
+The exact scales are:
+
+```text
+group A: mu=1/12, eta=7/36,  NO-RESIDUE scale -lambda_f=2mu=1/6
+group B: mu=3/26, eta=7/26,  NO-RESIDUE scale -lambda_f=2mu=3/13
+group C: mu=3/34, eta=11/34, NO-RESIDUE scale -lambda_f=2mu=3/17
+```
+
+In each case `2mu<eta`.  NO-RESIDUE is one raw equation on each of the 105
+branches, with orbit rank still to be computed; if the relevant exponent is
+absent it is vacuous.  Therefore the **first possible global count kill is
+order zero**, through the 34+1 moment checks.  The first named positive gate is
+NO-RESIDUE at `E=2mu`, conditional on support.  I would compute the moment and
+NO-RESIDUE matrices for the nine packets through the finite cutoffs
+`E<=1/4, 9/26, 11/34` for A, B, C respectively.  These cutoffs include all
+three restricted resonances and the first forced outer activation.
+
+`OPEN[TRIO-FIRST-COKERNEL]`: **bounded quantity:** nine formal packets; for each,
+return `(unknowns,equations,rank,cokernel)` at every actual exponent through the
+three cutoffs just stated, with all 105 branches and the outer/inner split.
+A kill of all nine proves only `D_min>=108`; the rebased census already has 76
+mixed survivors at `D=108` (`xmodel/census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md:431-450`).
+The trio is an excellent regression target and first client, but not a bespoke
+flagship.  A uniform moment-rank theorem is worth a flagship seat.
+
+### 2.3 Q3 — disposition of candidates (a)–(f)
+
+**(a) RAISE + RETYPE.**  Make this the filtered Hamiltonian/Brieskorn operator,
+not an abstract appeal to Picard--Fuchs theory.  With
+`D_g=g_y partial_x-g_x partial_y`, a mate solves `D_g f=1`; equivalently the
+Jacobian two-form has the appropriate exactness class in the quotient by
+`dg wedge d(Omega^0)`, with Moh's pole filtration imposed.  Its associated
+graded bottom page is BOTTOM-ODE and its higher/global pages are the moment
+conditions.  The cofinal invariant to seek is a filtered cokernel or
+valuated-matroid defect.
+
+**(b) LOWER the proposed conclusion, RAISE the data.**  A local dessin does not
+force `k=1`: bottom stars are broadly realisable.  Put the dessin blocks into
+the global moment matrix and test their Galois gluing.  A useful conditional
+cross-check is that the nonzero-factor orbit lengths for A, B, C are
+`A_2=18,13,17`.  If, and only if, one proves that such an orbit injects into
+distinct actual bottom discs, the permitted packets collapse to `k=18,13,17`
+and all three have `N=9`; this does not kill them.  The unproved injection is
+exactly the flag/place/series danger, so it is not used in any count below.
+
+**(c) LOWER as a standalone theorem; RETYPE as an accelerator.**  The canonical
+Hamiltonian connection already has vanishing `p`-curvature, so “prove zero
+`p`-curvature” is costume.  Good-prime sparse ranks, Cartier decompositions and
+Hensel lifts remain valuable diagnostics, provided every claimed kill is
+reconstructed over characteristic zero.  This agrees with the negative result
+in `xmodel/sol-pcurvature.md`.
+
+**(d) SPLIT.**  LOWER the generic semigroup claim: I checked the canonical
+approximate-root semigroup equation from Moh Proposition 3.1 on all 658 rows;
+it is automatic.  A full scalar Prop. 4.6 orbit/passport completion is also
+automatic under (7), retaining all 658 and all nine `(75,50)` rows.  RAISE a
+strictly richer *whole-tower approximate-root gluing* condition that retains
+sibling factors and coefficients.  Calling an unnamed scalar “the semigroup
+condition” no longer counts as a mechanism.
+
+**(e) RAISE + RETYPE.**  Replace floating high-order Newton iteration with exact
+lifting at several good primes, sparse rank discovery, and a rational
+cokernel/certificate.  Start from a live group and all its branches, not one
+local disc.  A long modular lift is a positive signal, never a map.
+
+**(f) CLOSE POSITIVELY at the arithmetic level; RETYPE the remainder.**  The
+printed (1)--(13) conditions plus formal (UNI) integrality are cofinally
+nonempty even with `N=6`, by the family below.  What remains open is actual
+packet and polynomial realisability.  Hence any all-degree proof must use data
+not present in the scalar skeleton.
+
+Here is the promised exact family.  For every `a>=0`, set `L=8a+5` and
+
+```text
+n=21L,  m=14L,  M_1=-14L,
+M_2=7(3L+1)/4,  M_3=21L-2,
+s=3,  V_2=1,  V_3=5.
+```
+
+Then `d_2=7L`, `d_3=7`, `d_4=1`.  The two windows are
+`7/2<5<=7` and `4L/(9L-1)<1<=5L`.  Direct substitution in Definition 5.1 gives
+
+```text
+delta_3=-1,
+delta_2=2(3L-1)/(3(5L-1)),
+delta_1=7/12.
+```
+
+Because `L=5 mod 8`, the reduced denominator increment is
+`A_2=3(5L-1)/4`; with `Q=V_3 d_2/d_3=5L`, condition (10) admits `V_2=1`.
+Next `A_1=den(A_2*7/12)` is 1 or 2.  If it is 2, (13) holds because
+`2|dV_2` and `2|(eV_2-1)`; if it is 1 both alternatives are automatic.
+Finally
+
+```text
+q=(1-delta_1)de/(d+e)=1/2,   u=V_3 K/d_3=5L.
+```
+
+Taking the **formal** (UNI) multiplier `k=12` gives `kV_2<=u` and `N=6`.
+The degrees begin `105,273,441,609,...` and are unbounded.  I checked the
+algebra separately and ran the first 21 members through the exact census
+implementation, all passing.  This is a theorem about the printed numerical
+skeleton and formal knapsack only.  It neither constructs 12 distinct actual
+discs nor a Keller map.
+
+The genuinely new cross-connection is now visible: the global interpolation
+conditions are Reed--Solomon parity checks whose differentiated rows recover
+the banked STAR-SUM identities on the bottom associated graded
+(`xmodel/time-function-endgame-review-sol56-20260902.md:236-261`).  The growing
+parity-check block has size `n-m=7L`, whereas the proper bottom block can remain
+fixed at formal `N=6`; the reducible analysis says that the non-proper block
+contributes zero to `N` but contains all reducibility data (`notes.md:20709-20713`).
+Thus the object that may grow with degree is not a boundary charge but the
+minimum-distance/valuated-rank defect of a differential evaluation code, with
+the zero-charge non-proper coordinates retained.
+
+### 2.4 Q4 — the machine filter
+
+Build a **quotient-algebra moment engine**, initially for `s=3`.  It should take
+one exact skeleton plus a typed branch packet, not merely `(n,m,M,V)`, and run:
+
+1. Validate (1)--(13), exact pinned integrality, branch labels, exponent
+   semigroup and outer/inner ownership.  Reject missing route-to-state data.
+2. Over `Q(c,x)`, form `B=Q(c,x)[y]/(g-c)` in a declared generator order.
+   Compute `g_y^{-1}` by extended Euclid on the squarefree component and form
+   `nabla`.  Split discriminant/vanished-pivot branches rather than dividing
+   through them.
+3. Solve/prolong `nabla F=1/g_y` sparsely.  Compute the 35 parity coordinates
+   at `D=105` either as high-`y` remainders or as
+   `Tr_B(F y^r/g_y)`, so no explicit root expansion or 105-term interpolation
+   is required.
+4. Enforce all 71 coefficient channels of `F=sum_(j=0)^70 f_j(x)y^j` against
+   the allowed polynomial degree polygon, exponent by exponent.  Record fresh
+   `g` coefficients, gauge variables, equations, exact rank and cokernel; never
+   infer a kill from raw equation count alone.
+5. Discover rank over two or three good primes, then reconstruct a nonzero
+   minor or left-kernel functional over `Q`.  On exceptional minors, extract
+   the intended ideal component and run positive and negative controls before
+   any saturation claim.
+
+The smallest build worth doing this week supports the nine `D=105` packets and
+the four fixed-ray values `L=5,13,21,29`, through the first bottom-separation
+graded page; the largest ray test has `7L-1=202` initial vanishing rows.  It emits
+a JSON certificate per exponent with the ring map, support provenance,
+`(variables,equations,rank,cokernel)`, pivot numerator and exceptional ideal.
+That makes a finite computation reusable in an all-template proof.
+
+Positive control: the tame Keller pairs `(f,g)=(y,x+y^k)` must pass and recover
+the interpolant `y`.  Negative controls: `g=x^j+y^k`, `j>=2`, must fail global
+polynomial interpolation by the exact leading-degree obstruction, and
+`g=y^2-x^2-x` must fail the NO-RESIDUE channel.  These controls catch the two
+most likely vacuous successes: solving only in a completed local ring and
+silently dropping the polynomial-in-`x` constraint.  The banked exact controls
+and derivation are at
+`xmodel/time-function-endgame-review-sol56-20260902.md:713-727`.
+
+## 3. Reranked bottlenecks and attacks
+
+### 3.1 Proof bottlenecks
+
+1. **Uniform global filtered cokernel.**  Prove that the differential moment
+   code has a nonzero syndrome/cokernel on every admissible all-degree template,
+   or at least on every cofinal family.  This is now the theorem-sized obstacle.
+2. **Whole-tower coefficient and sibling gluing.**  Recover an exact condition
+   that explains Moh's 652-row discrepancy.  Scalar characteristic-semigroup
+   and passport data have just failed this test; the remaining datum must see
+   simultaneous defining equations or expose an error in p. 202.
+3. **Actual orbit packet.**  Determine which formal `k` choices are geometric:
+   map cyclic factors to distinct flags/discs, retain the fixed-zero factors,
+   and prove the multiplicities are counted once.  Without this, neither (UNI)
+   nor mixed knapsack is attainment.
+4. **Template extraction.**  Convert finite quotient-algebra computations into
+   a theorem on symbolic divisor-chain/semigroup templates.  A table through
+   `D=10^6` would still not be an all-degree proof.
+5. **Algebraisation at infinity.**  If the formal global system survives, prove
+   that its series terminate with the required polynomial degree bounds.  This
+   is where a counterexample construction must ultimately succeed and where a
+   proof may obtain its last obstruction.
+
+The old ordering put “find a boundary ceiling” ahead of these.  That item is
+closed negatively, not merely stalled.
+
+### 3.2 Disproof bottlenecks
+
+1. Produce one exact, all-branch, globally compatible Puiseux lift for
+   `D=105` group A with `k=12`, satisfying moments and NO-RESIDUE.
+2. Stabilize the lift on at least the next member `L=13` of the fixed-`N=6`
+   family and identify a parametric recurrence rather than isolated numerical
+   coincidences.
+3. Algebraize/terminate the lift to polynomials and retain the necessary
+   non-proper block.
+4. Verify nonzero constant Jacobian and then exhibit nonproperness/a collision.
+
+The first two would be the campaign's first serious positive evidence above
+degree 100.  They would still not be a counterexample.  The last two are the
+actual threshold.
+
+### 3.3 Strongest proof attack
+
+Exploit the determinant structure of the global moment code.  Before
+differentiation, its parity-check matrix is generalized Vandermonde; its minors
+are Vandermonde products times powers of `g_y(tau_i)`.  The Moh tree supplies
+valuations of root differences.  Therefore the leading rank problem is a
+tropical determinant/minimum-weight matching problem on the branch tree, and
+the exact next coefficient decides ties.  This is far more structured than a
+generic 105-by-unknown matrix.
+
+The candidate uniform theorem is a **valuated-MDS defect**: for a counterexample
+packet, the prescribed valuations of the primitive vector force a nonzero
+parity syndrome before the allowed coefficient filtration can absorb it.  On
+the fixed family, the number of parity coordinates grows as `n-m=7L`, while
+the formal `N=6`, `V_2=1`, cubic bottom packet can be held at 12 discs (36
+proper `g` roots).  A proof must explicitly retain the remaining non-proper
+coordinates; if they always repair the parity syndromes, their Schur complement
+is the invariant to study.  This connects the proper/non-proper decomposition
+to coding-theoretic minimum distance without pretending that the zero-`N`
+block is absent (`AUDIT.md:15441-15470`).
+
+The attack is: compute the associated-graded moment matrix symbolically for
+`L=5,13,21,29`; identify its minimum-weight bases; conjecture the stable minor
+or left-kernel functional; prove its valuation and leading coefficient for
+general `L=8a+5`; then lift the associated-graded nonvanishing through the
+connection filtration.  A single certified cofinal obstruction beats any
+finite degree census.  Conversely, a stable full-rank Schur complement tells
+the counterexample lane exactly which non-proper variables supply the missing
+freedom.
+
+### 3.4 Strongest counterexample attack
+
+Start with group A, `D=105,k=12`, because it is the first point of the unbounded
+family, has the smallest packet reaching `N=6`, and uses the explicit cubic
+dessin above.  Instantiate the complete Galois-compatible bottom packet, solve
+the 34+1 global moment equations and NO-RESIDUE over each of
+`F_211,F_223,F_227`, and Hensel-lift exponent by exponent through `E=1/4`.
+Reject any pivot whose characteristic-zero numerator reconstructs to zero.
+If all three primes give the same dimension and an exact rational lift, repeat
+at `L=13`; search the two solutions for a recurrence in `L`.  Each desk run is
+capped at 8 minutes, 3.5 GB and 2,000 active variables; above that, retain only
+the linear Schur/cokernel projection.
+
+There is also a sharp Q1 falsifier.  The excess row
+`(75,50,M_2,V_2)=(75,50,40,1)` has `A_1=2` and an exact cyclic bottom solution.
+For `b!=0`,
+
+```text
+p(pi)=pi^3+(3b/2)pi,       q(pi)=pi^2+b,
+D(3,2,p,q)=-3b^2,          Res(p,q)=b^3/4,
+disc(p)=-27b^3/2,           disc(q)=-4b.
+```
+
+Thus the roots are squarefree/coprime and have the required odd/even `C_2`
+symmetry.  Extending this witness through its one remaining major level is the
+cheapest attempt to refute every proposed *local* missing filter.  It does not
+yet refute a coherent all-sibling or global-interpolation condition.
+
+The decisive interpretation is three-valued: an exact cokernel certificate is
+a real kill; a stable high-order lift is construction evidence and determines
+the next member to test; inconsistent prime dimensions indicate an exceptional
+component that must be split, not averaged.  No finite lift is polynomial
+attainment.
+
+## 4. Idea cards
+
+### Card 1 — MOMENT-CODE / FILTERED-HAMILTONIAN ENGINE
+
+**Claim/avenue.**  The global Keller-mate condition is an exact differential
+Reed--Solomon membership problem in the finite algebra `B`; its filtered
+cokernel may be the all-degree obstruction.
+
+**Dependencies.**  JAC-FIBRE; a typed orbit packet; the complete exponent
+support and outer/inner ownership; exact quotient-ring maps.
+
+**Cheapest discriminator.**  Build the 34 vanishings plus one monic row for the
+nine `D=105` packets, prolong through the three finite cutoffs in §2.2, and
+cross-check the trace implementation against explicit Lagrange interpolation
+on a small tame control.
+
+**Outcomes.**  A nonzero exact left-cokernel functional kills that packet and
+offers a theorem candidate.  Compatible ranks hand a reduced affine fibre to
+the lifting lane.  If every row reduces to LOCAL-KELLER/STAR-SUM, the chosen
+filtration is costume and must be enriched by polynomial coefficient bounds.
+
+**Stop condition.**  Stop the first build after all nine certificates and the
+three controls, or immediately if the trace and coefficient-coordinate
+implementations disagree.  Expected information gain: **very high**; it tests
+the actual global obstruction and produces reusable certificates.
+
+### Card 2 — FIXED-`N` COFINAL FAMILY / VALUATED-MDS
+
+**Claim/avenue.**  The family `L=8a+5` is an adversarial all-degree laboratory.
+Its boundary/dessin data stay small while the global parity block grows, so a
+stable valuated-matroid defect could prove a uniform obstruction.
+
+**Dependencies.**  Card 1's order-zero matrix, the proper/non-proper split, and
+tree valuations of every root difference.  It does not assume that 12 formal
+discs are actual.
+
+**Cheapest discriminator.**  For `L=5,13,21,29`, compute the tropical ranks and
+then exact leading ranks of the first `7L-1` vanishing checks on the first
+bottom-separation page.  The largest case has 202 such rows.
+
+**Outcomes.**  Growing nonzero syndrome/minor suggests a cofinal proof and names
+the induction invariant.  Full rank supplied by the non-proper Schur block
+identifies the counterexample construction interface.  Constant zero defect
+means this associated graded is too weak.
+
+**Stop condition.**  Stop after four members if the rank defect and its
+minimum-weight basis pattern neither stabilize nor separate proper from
+non-proper data.  `OPEN[FAMILY-MOMENT-DEFECT]`: **bounded quantity:** these four
+family members, at most 202 parity rows each, through one graded separation
+page.  Expected information gain: **very high**, because either outcome speaks
+to unbounded degree rather than just `D=105`.
+
+### Card 3 — MOH TABLE / WHOLE-TOWER REALISATION
+
+**Claim/avenue.**  Moh's 658-to-6 reduction was either a coherent coefficient
+and sibling-gluing computation not captured by (1)--(13), or it was erroneous;
+ordinary scalar semigroup/passport gates do not explain it.
+
+**Dependencies.**  The verified PDF, `box/moh_skeleton_full.py`, Propositions
+3.1, 4.6, 5.3, 5.6 and Appendix II.  Every inferred program action is labelled
+source-unverified until code or a printed implication is found.
+
+**Cheapest discriminator.**  Work only on the nine `(75,50)` rows.  Construct
+the Prop. 4.6 differential polynomials for every sibling factor and glue the
+two levels through the approximate-root recurrence.  The six-row table's two
+`M_2=55` rows are positive controls; the seven other local rows are negative
+targets.  Also source-audit the measured candidate `A_{s-1}|(n-m)`, which leaves
+181 rows/29 classes and uniquely selects the two correct `(75,50)` rows but is
+currently unlicensed.
+
+**Outcomes.**  An exact source-backed/gluing obstruction that preserves the two
+controls is a plausible reconstruction and can be tested on all 658.  If the
+explicit `M_2=40,V_2=1` witness glues, the p. 202 completeness claim becomes
+seriously doubtful.  If all nine glue locally but fail only in the global
+moment engine, the “missing program” is not a separate all-degree mechanism.
+
+**Stop condition.**  Stop after the nine-row coefficient systems and a direct
+Appendix-II dependency graph; do not tune another scalar predicate to the six.
+Expected information gain: **high** for historical correctness and medium for
+the all-degree theorem.
