+### 2.2 Q2 — the `D = 105` trio
+
+All three groups have `(n,m,K,d,e,V_2)=(105,70,35,2,3,1)` and hence the
+same order-zero cubic dessin, after affine/scalar normalization:
+
+```text
+p_g(pi)=pi^3-pi,       p_f(pi)=pi^2-2/3.
+```
+
+Order zero cannot distinguish them and cannot kill them.  The useful arithmetic
+is instead:
+
+| group | `(M_2,V_3)` | `delta_2` | `delta_1` | `q` | formal packets in `6<=N<=16` |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| A | `(28,5)` | `7/18` | `7/12` | `1/2` | `k=12,14,16,18,20,22,24` |
+| B | `(28,6)` | `2/13` | `11/26` | `9/13` | `k=13` |
+| C | `(40,4)` | `4/17` | `19/34` | `9/17` | `k=17` |
+
+Thus there are nine formal (UNI) packet cases, not merely three rows.  “Formal”
+is essential: `k` records a numerical choice within the bottom capacity; it is
+not a count of proved actual exits or an attainment statement.
+
+The cheapest exact global discriminator avoids constructing a 105-term
+Lagrange polynomial.  For monic `h(z)=g(x,z)-c=prod_i(z-tau_i)` and branch
+primitives `I_i`, let `H` be their degree-`<105` interpolant and set
+
+```text
+S_r = sum_i I_i tau_i^r / h'(tau_i).
+```
+
+The partial-fraction identity
+
+```text
+H(z)/h(z) = sum_i I_i/[h'(tau_i)(z-tau_i)]
+          = sum_(r>=0) S_r z^(-r-1)
+```
+
+shows that a **monic degree-70** mate satisfies exactly 34 degree vanishings
+`S_0=...=S_33=0` and one normalization `S_34=1`.  At every positive Puiseux
+order, the corresponding 35 equations are homogeneous.  This is a differential
+generalized Reed--Solomon parity check.  It is equivalent to projecting the
+quotient-algebra solution `F` to its 34 forbidden high-`y` coordinates and its
+one leading coordinate.  The fibre primitive and global interpolation identity
+are exact (`xmodel/time-function-endgame-review-sol56-20260902.md:43-60`), while
+the same review warns that local completed-series membership is not global
+polynomiality (`ibid.:103-130`).
+
+This supplies the requested condition count, but **not** an honest unknown
+count before the full branch packet and exponent support are supplied.  The
+restricted bottom operator has seven coefficient unknowns and five equations:
+generic rank 5, kernel 2, cokernel 0; at `E in {mu,2mu,3mu}` it has rank 4,
+kernel 3, cokernel 1.  That is a local associated-graded calculation, not the
+global count.  Outer roots already enlarge the coefficient spaces and the
+first-exponent semigroup has not been established
+(`xmodel/time-function-endgame-review-sol56-20260902.md:489-520,574-607`).
+Accordingly, a lane that prints “unknowns minus conditions” without those two
+inputs has not answered Q2.
+
+The exact scales are:
+
+```text
+group A: mu=1/12, eta=7/36,  NO-RESIDUE scale -lambda_f=2mu=1/6
+group B: mu=3/26, eta=7/26,  NO-RESIDUE scale -lambda_f=2mu=3/13
+group C: mu=3/34, eta=11/34, NO-RESIDUE scale -lambda_f=2mu=3/17
+```
+
+In each case `2mu<eta`.  NO-RESIDUE is one raw equation on each of the 105
+branches, with orbit rank still to be computed; if the relevant exponent is
+absent it is vacuous.  Therefore the **first possible global count kill is
+order zero**, through the 34+1 moment checks.  The first named positive gate is
+NO-RESIDUE at `E=2mu`, conditional on support.  I would compute the moment and
+NO-RESIDUE matrices for the nine packets through the finite cutoffs
+`E<=1/4, 9/26, 11/34` for A, B, C respectively.  These cutoffs include all
+three restricted resonances and the first forced outer activation.
+
+`OPEN[TRIO-FIRST-COKERNEL]`: **bounded quantity:** nine formal packets; for each,
+return `(unknowns,equations,rank,cokernel)` at every actual exponent through the
+three cutoffs just stated, with all 105 branches and the outer/inner split.
+A kill of all nine proves only `D_min>=108`; the rebased census already has 76
+mixed survivors at `D=108` (`xmodel/census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md:431-450`).
+The trio is an excellent regression target and first client, but not a bespoke
+flagship.  A uniform moment-rank theorem is worth a flagship seat.
