+### 2.4 Q4 — the machine filter
+
+Build a **quotient-algebra moment engine**, initially for `s=3`.  It should take
+one exact skeleton plus a typed branch packet, not merely `(n,m,M,V)`, and run:
+
+1. Validate (1)--(13), exact pinned integrality, branch labels, exponent
+   semigroup and outer/inner ownership.  Reject missing route-to-state data.
+2. Over `Q(c,x)`, form `B=Q(c,x)[y]/(g-c)` in a declared generator order.
+   Compute `g_y^{-1}` by extended Euclid on the squarefree component and form
+   `nabla`.  Split discriminant/vanished-pivot branches rather than dividing
+   through them.
+3. Solve/prolong `nabla F=1/g_y` sparsely.  Compute the 35 parity coordinates
+   at `D=105` either as high-`y` remainders or as
+   `Tr_B(F y^r/g_y)`, so no explicit root expansion or 105-term interpolation
+   is required.
+4. Enforce all 71 coefficient channels of `F=sum_(j=0)^70 f_j(x)y^j` against
+   the allowed polynomial degree polygon, exponent by exponent.  Record fresh
+   `g` coefficients, gauge variables, equations, exact rank and cokernel; never
+   infer a kill from raw equation count alone.
+5. Discover rank over two or three good primes, then reconstruct a nonzero
+   minor or left-kernel functional over `Q`.  On exceptional minors, extract
+   the intended ideal component and run positive and negative controls before
+   any saturation claim.
+
+The smallest build worth doing this week supports the nine `D=105` packets and
+the four fixed-ray values `L=5,13,21,29`, through the first bottom-separation
+graded page; the largest ray test has `7L-1=202` initial vanishing rows.  It emits
+a JSON certificate per exponent with the ring map, support provenance,
+`(variables,equations,rank,cokernel)`, pivot numerator and exceptional ideal.
+That makes a finite computation reusable in an all-template proof.
+
+Positive control: the tame Keller pairs `(f,g)=(y,x+y^k)` must pass and recover
+the interpolant `y`.  Negative controls: `g=x^j+y^k`, `j>=2`, must fail global
+polynomial interpolation by the exact leading-degree obstruction, and
+`g=y^2-x^2-x` must fail the NO-RESIDUE channel.  These controls catch the two
+most likely vacuous successes: solving only in a completed local ring and
+silently dropping the polynomial-in-`x` constraint.  The banked exact controls
+and derivation are at
+`xmodel/time-function-endgame-review-sol56-20260902.md:713-727`.
